Farmer Smith's farm is more than twice Farmer Brown's farm. Twice Farmer Brown’s farm is 200 * 2 = 400 acres. Farmer Smith's farm is 100 acres *more* than that, so it is 400 + 100 = 500 acres.

The two farms together have 200 + 500 = 700 acres.

\boxed{700}

completions_12:
John drinks 1/3 of a bottle of water every half hour. An extreme sudoku takes 4 * 45 minutes = 180 minutes.  Since he drinks 1/3 of a bottle every half hour, and there are two half hour periods in an hour, he drinks 2 * (1/3) = 2/3 of a bottle per hour.  Over 180 minutes (3 hours), he drinks 3 * (2/3) = 2 bottles of water.

Alternatively, 180 minutes / 30 minutes per bottle = 6 half-hour periods.  Therefore, he drinks 6 * (1/3) = 2 bottles of water.

\boxed{2}

